  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Art Illustration Festival: Gather gift boxes (宝可梦艺术插画庆典 聚) came out on 6 December 2024 in two versions, a Poké Ball box and a Level Ball box, the Level Ball's first time as a box; each ball can be kept for storage or display. Each box held one art illustration holo, one of nine made in equal numbers and all drawn by the same artist: Riolu, Swablu, Duskull, Bidoof, Pikachu, Turtwig, Paras, Poochyena and Mareep. Laid out three by three in number order, the nine cards make one picture of the nine Pokémon together. Each box also held a Poké Ball or Level Ball holo card, which with luck was replaced by a random special-art Trainer holo, and a random 25-card Shadow of the Blue Sea pack.\n\nThe nine art cards are numbered out of 11 with the Poké Ball and Level Ball cards; the special-art Trainers Allister, Raihan, Piers, Opal and Melony are numbered past it, up to 016.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Pikachu & Eevee quicksand pendant box and Art Illustration Festival: Gather (22 November 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/15625.html"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"CSYC\" mark at the bottom left, and a number out of 011",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Pikachu & Eevee quicksand pendant box and Art Illustration Festival: Gather (22 November 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/15625.html"
      }
    ]
  },
